# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UMArm Koopman compliance-control workspace — ignore rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ESP-IDF build trees (firmware/tle/build, firmware/legacy/build_7mm, ...).
# The *prebuilt* images we deliberately keep live in firmware/images/ and are
# not matched by these patterns.
build/
build*/
!firmware/images/
sdkconfig.old
*.elf
*.map

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.venv*/
venv/

# Hardware-test and bench output. Anything under hw_tests/results/ is bulk
# measurement data: it is regenerated by re-running the bench, never reviewed
# in a diff.  Written as a glob over the contents rather than as the directory
# itself, because git will not re-include a file inside an excluded directory
# and the exceptions below have to work.
hw_tests/results/*

# ... with one class of exception: the records that *calibration constants in
# the source cite by name*. Re-running the bench does not regenerate those, it
# produces a different arm pose set, after which the committed numbers would
# have no auditable origin. Keep the campaign and its reduction.
!hw_tests/results/drive_2026-08-21.json
!hw_tests/results/axis_analysis_2026-08-21.json
!hw_tests/results/axis_analysis_2026-08-21.md
!hw_tests/results/gui_kinematics_2026-08-21.json

# Marker locks are minted per Motive session against that session's marker
# labels. A committed lock file would be registered against plates as they were
# on some past afternoon, and a stale lock fails every frame's template gate --
# loudly, but for a reason nobody would look for in a checked-in file.
UMArm_MOCAP/templates/canarm_locks.json
logs/
*.log
reports/*.csv
real_system_data_collection/

# A mechanical fit's best-so-far checkpoint while it runs (digital_twin.mech_fit
# progress_path).  Only a complete fit is promoted onto canarm_mech.json.
digital_twin/checkpoints/*.running.json

# Large recorded data of any provenance
*.npz
*.jsonl
*.zip

# Editor / OS
.vs/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Collection sessions: 274k cycles is ~300 MB of JSONL per session, and the
# recordings are regenerated by re-running the bench, never reviewed in a diff.
data/session_*/
data/fit/*.log
data/*.log
data/*.err

# Rendered video. The side-by-side deliverable is ~33 MB; keep the frame that
# documents it and the JSON that carries its numbers, not the mp4.
*.mp4
!hw_tests/media/*.jpg

# Regenerated controller rollouts and temporary training checkpoints. The
# selected model, coverage summary, benchmark JSON and final videos are kept.
control/data/
control/checkpoints/*.running.pt
!deliverable/dynamic_control/soft_*.mp4

# Reproducible figure-eight compliance experiments and trained readouts.
!data/compliance_*/*.npz
!deliverable/fig8_compliance_*/*.npz
!deliverable/fig8_compliance_*/*.mp4
RL PPO/runs/
RL PPO/eval/
